From: Soe Thura <6492082+thixpin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:29:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] Function analysis: stop at the size limit

Function::Analyze looped while data <= dataEnd, so it read and included one word past the size
it was given. With a size that ends at the next known function, that word is the next
function's first instruction. In Forza Motorsport 4 a two-entry stack-probe routine became two
overlapping functions.
---
 XenonAnalyse/function.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/XenonAnalyse/function.cpp b/XenonAnalyse/function.cpp
index 34add40..4831c85 100644
--- a/XenonAnalyse/function.cpp
+++ b/XenonAnalyse/function.cpp
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ Function Function::Analyze(const void* code, size_t size, size_t base)
     #define RESTORE_DATA() if (!blockStack.empty()) data = (dataStart + ((blocks[blockStack.back()].base + blocks[blockStack.back()].size) / sizeof(*data))) - 1; // continue adds one
 
     // TODO: Branch fallthrough
-    for (; data <= dataEnd ; ++data)
+    for (; data < dataEnd ; ++data)
     {
         const size_t addr = base + ((data - dataStart) * sizeof(*data));
         if (blockStack.empty())
